--- Overview
Adds two new buckets to the BadgerDB-backed database: one for precomputed per-prefix summaries and one for database metadata, such as how the summaries were computed. The database.DB interface gains matching methods.

--- Key Changes
  * internal/database (ifc.go, README)
    * Extended the DB interface with SetSummary, DeleteSummary, ScanSummaries, SetMeta and GetMeta.
  * internal/database/badgerdb
    * Added the summaryBucket (0xf4) and metaBucket (0xf5) key prefixes and updated the bucket layout docs from 4 to 6 buckets.
    * SetSummary: writes a summary entry and supports batched writes. It rejects writes on read-only databases.
    * DeleteSummary: deletes exactKey and all descendants under childPrefix, leaving sibling prefixes alone (for example, \x00a-b survives deleting \x00a).
    * ScanSummaries: walks keys in order starting at exactKey and stops at the first key outside exactKey/childPrefix. With both empty, it scans the whole bucket. The visitor can return false to stop early.
    * SetMeta / GetMeta: store and read metadata entries. Reading a missing key returns an empty buffer, not an error.
  * Tests
    * Added TestSummariesAndMeta, which covers batched and unbatched writes, persistence after reopening, read-only meta reads, missing meta keys, subtree scans that exclude siblings, and subtree deletes.

--- Breaking Changes
Every implementation of database.DB must now provide the five new methods. The package is internal and BadgerDB is the only implementation in this diff, so external users are not affected.
